<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Tungning</h1><p class="st-meta">1661 CE – 1683 CE · capital Tungning (Tainan)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Ming loyalist kingdom of Koxinga and his heirs on Taiwan, which drove out the Dutch and became the first Han Chinese state on the island.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koxinga">Koxinga</a> (<a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/zheng-wang-shichong">Zheng</a> Chenggong), son of the merchant-admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-zhilong">Zheng Zhilong</a>, led Ming loyalist forces on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujian">Fujian</a> coast after 1646. After a failed attack on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a> in 1659 he sought a new base, invaded <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dutch-formosa">Dutch Formosa</a> in 1661 and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-zeelandia-taiwan">Fort Zeelandia</a> in 1662, but died a few months later.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-jing">Zheng Jing</a> and the minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chen-yonghua">Chen Yonghua</a> built a Chinese-style administration at Tungning (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tainan">Tainan</a>), founded the first Confucian temple and schools on <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-china">Taiwan</a> in 1666, settled soldiers on farmland and traded with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, South-east Asia and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">English East India Company</a>. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/zheng-wang-shichong">Zheng</a> Jing joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revolt-of-the-three-feudatories">Revolt of the Three Feudatories</a> in 1674 and occupied coastal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujian">Fujian</a> for a time.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-jing">Zheng Jing's</a> death in 1681, court factions placed his young son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-keshuang">Zheng Keshuang</a> on the throne. In 1683 the Qing admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shi-lang">Shi Lang</a> destroyed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/zheng-wang-shichong">Zheng</a> fleet at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penghu">Penghu</a>, and Zheng Keshuang surrendered. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-china">Taiwan</a> became a prefecture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujian">Fujian</a> under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-tungning.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Tungning" width="320" height="480"><figcaption>Image: Luuva · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdom_of_Tungning.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1661 CE – 1683 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tungning (Tainan)</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Koxinga (Zheng Chenggong), Zheng Jing, Zheng Keshuang</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Chinese folk religion, Confucianism, Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hokkien, Middle Mandarin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/taiwan">Taiwan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tungning, Zheng dynasty, Kingdom of Formosa</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1672&amp;focus=kingdom-of-tungning" aria-label="Kingdom of Tungning on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7890 1325 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Tungning lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8210 1581L8056 1267M8210 1581L7567 1068M8210 1581L8210 1585"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8056 1267h0M7567 1068h0M8210 1585h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8210 1581h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8210 1581h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?